1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,925
THERE IS NO RELATION
TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

3
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:43,961
EPISODE 1

4
00:00:57,391 --> 00:01:01,228
Good morning! Hey, Daniel!

5
00:01:05,941 --> 00:01:06,942
KARIN'S SWEET POTATO FARM

6
00:01:08,402 --> 00:01:11,446
NO OVERTIME - TEMP WORKER
FIRST-TIMERS WELCOME

7
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:15,951
-Good morning!
-Whoa. [coughs]

8
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:17,369
Hey,

9
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:18,745
-good morning…
-I brought you water.

10
00:01:18,829 --> 00:01:19,830
Thank you.

11
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:23,584
But, uh, I wish
you brought some help instead.

12
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:26,962
I wish I could have brought
a hundred people to help.

13
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:31,258
But it's hard to find anyone who wants
to do farm work with intensive labor.

14
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:38,640
[sighs] That's why the both of us
will work extra hard. Okay?

15
00:01:38,724 --> 00:01:40,017
[coughs] What?

16
00:01:41,351 --> 00:01:42,603
That's too hard!

17
00:01:42,686 --> 00:01:46,440
You really expect us to work
this entire field ourselves?

18
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:50,152
Really? We can't.

19
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:52,779
It's impossible! [voice echoes]

20
00:01:52,863 --> 00:01:54,489
Fine, then. We'll just get

21
00:01:54,573 --> 00:01:56,366
-a thousand meters or so done.
-What?

22
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:59,661
That's not much. All right.
Time's a-ticking. Let's move it.

23
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:01,204
-Come on.
-[groans]

24
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:07,627
-[in German] I'm dying out here.
-[in English] Huh? What was that?

25
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:09,629
Uh, the sky's nice and clear.

26
00:02:11,715 --> 00:02:13,425
What a nice day!

27
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,157
Good morning.

28
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:40,160
Ah! Good morning, Grandma!

29
00:03:07,187 --> 00:03:09,064
[in Korean] The pictures are turning out
great here.

30
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:11,191
[friend 1] Yeah?
Hey, let's take one together.

31
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:13,485
Sure, let's get someone to take it for us.

32
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:18,490
Would you like me to take it for you?

33
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:20,325
-[friend 2] Oh, would you?
-Yeah.

34
00:03:20,409 --> 00:03:22,911
Then could you take one of us together?
Thank you.

35
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:26,289
Hey, isn't he the CEO of Y:SPACE?

36
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:27,374
Lee Yubin?

37
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:29,209
-[friend 1] Whoa, is that really him?
-Yeah!

38
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:32,546
-[friend 1] No way. That's insane.
-[friend 2] Wow, how cool! [chuckles]

39
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:38,343
Hey, that came out really pretty.

40
00:03:38,427 --> 00:03:40,720
[friend 2] "Pretty"? Thank you.

41
00:03:40,804 --> 00:03:43,890
Oh, my gosh, he said we look pretty!
Hey, let's see.

42
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:46,935
Huh?

43
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:48,019
What is this?

44
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:50,772
MADE IT TO MONÉA, THE 2025 KME
DESIGN AWARD WINNER, AT OPENING!

45
00:03:50,856 --> 00:03:52,190
NO WAY, DID YOU SEE LEE YUBIN?

46
00:03:52,274 --> 00:03:53,817
YES! HE'S WAY TOO HOT
TO BE A SPATIAL DESIGNER

47
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:08,665
We displayed these individually.
As for the candles…

48
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:11,001
Excuse me for a sec.

49
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:12,961
Boss. Hey,
what are you doing here so early?

50
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:15,297
Huh? The opening's
not for another two hours.

51
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,468
They're from the head office.
This is our CEO, Lee Yubin.

52
00:04:19,551 --> 00:04:21,511
Why don't you two
introduce yourselves and…

53
00:04:21,595 --> 00:04:24,473
Wow. Look at you, boss.
Working so hard. [chuckles]

54
00:04:24,556 --> 00:04:26,224
You're already… What? What is it?

55
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:29,102
It's a little crooked…

56
00:04:29,186 --> 00:04:31,396
Excuse me. Could you make sure
these are lined up properly?

57
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,522
Yeah.

58
00:04:32,606 --> 00:04:34,483
You haven't had your coffee yet, have you?

59
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:36,735
Yeah, let's go grab a nice,
hot cup of coffee…

60
00:04:37,486 --> 00:04:39,863
Hey, Yubin. Wait, boss. Yubin!

61
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:42,532
-How about some coffee?
-Good evening, sir.

62
00:04:42,616 --> 00:04:44,785
Come on, have some coffee!

63
00:04:49,331 --> 00:04:51,333
-Hey.
-Yeah?

64
00:04:51,416 --> 00:04:52,417
What…

65
00:04:54,628 --> 00:04:55,629
What is that?

66
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:57,631
Wait, you think…

67
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:01,426
You think that color goes
with the rest of the space?

68
00:05:01,510 --> 00:05:04,054
You really think a red table belongs here?

69
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:08,183
Just let it slide just this once,
all right?

70
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:11,770
The client specifically asked for it.
They're the one paying--

71
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:16,149
Whoa, boss! How are we supposed
to defy the almighty client?

72
00:05:16,233 --> 00:05:18,360
That thing's expensive! Please don't.

73
00:05:19,402 --> 00:05:21,404
What's the condition
in our client contracts?

74
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:27,494
"Lee Yubin's designs are
never, ever to be altered."

75
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:32,165
[inhales sharply] Take it away.

76
00:05:41,675 --> 00:05:43,134
I learn so much from you every day.

77
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:51,935
SPATIAL DESIGN GRAND PRIZE
KOREAN ARCHITECTURE ASSOCIATION

78
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:53,019
SPATIAL DESIGN AWARD - WINNER

79
00:05:53,103 --> 00:05:54,104
2023 GARDEN DESIGN AWARD

80
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:55,480
ASSOCIATION OF ARCHITECTS
SPECIAL AWARD

81
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:17,669
Come on, boss. You've got to learn
to enjoy yourself once a project's over.

82
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:19,796
This was our first team dinner
in six months.

83
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,715
You could've shown up.

84
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:24,342
Have you ever seen me at team dinners?

85
00:06:24,426 --> 00:06:26,887
All a CEO needs to do is
keep his mouth shut and pick up the bill.

86
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:28,221
Why make everyone uncomfortable?

87
00:06:28,305 --> 00:06:29,472
You're so uptight.

88
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,475
[sighs] Ease up a little, will you?

89
00:06:32,559 --> 00:06:34,436
That way, the staff might
actually follow you…

90
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:35,562
Ease up?

91
00:06:37,022 --> 00:06:38,064
Hey.

92
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:42,652
We put our company's reputation
on the line to win this project.

93
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:45,196
All right? And we beat
100-to-1 odds to get it, no less.

94
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,740
Giving it all might still fall short.

95
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,742
-But you want me to ease up?
-All right.

96
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:50,035
Yeah, you're right.

97
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:54,164
Once this project's finished,
your name's going global.

98
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,582
I know that.

99
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,501
Here you go.

100
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:00,587
Cheers.

101
00:07:06,051 --> 00:07:10,388
Now that the investors are
finally done with their review,

102
00:07:10,472 --> 00:07:12,057
looks like all that's left
is for us to sign!

103
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,600
Hey, but this…

104
00:07:15,602 --> 00:07:17,395
Are you sure this is legit?

105
00:07:17,479 --> 00:07:20,482
-Huh?
-I mean, this is a huge project,

106
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:23,777
and they're investing
in a startup like us?

107
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,988
-Does that even make sense?
-Lee Yubin.

108
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,950
You, our CEO. That's who they believe in.

109
00:07:31,910 --> 00:07:33,912
The legal review's totally clear.
Everything checks out.

110
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:38,458
-Good work.
-[chuckles]

111
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:42,712
Oh, the contract.
Here, you should look it over too.

112
00:07:43,546 --> 00:07:45,590
It's fine.
I'm sure you've handled it just fine.

113
00:07:46,508 --> 00:07:47,509
Nah, come on.

114
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:49,260
I'm busy, man. You take care of it.

115
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:52,097
All right.

116
00:07:52,806 --> 00:07:57,644
Don't worry about this kind of thing.
You just focus on the design work, okay?

117
00:07:57,727 --> 00:08:00,563
I'll take care
of all the tedious stuff like this.

118
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:02,524
Oh, and this.

119
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:05,902
-Well, it was on my desk.
-What is it?

120
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:07,654
I think the newbie got confused.

121
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:09,739
What's this? Japan?

122
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:16,496
Oh, sorry. I thought it was for me
and opened it.

123
00:08:17,414 --> 00:08:21,501
Hey, looks like your father
left you some land in Japan.

124
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,923
INFORMATION REGARDING
YOUR UNSETTLED INHERITANCE

125
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:28,007
[Yubin] You speak Japanese?

126
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:31,886
Well, Japan is a major market for us.

127
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:34,431
I had a quick look, and it's an island.

128
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:38,643
Imagine turning that island into a resort.

129
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:40,186
Huh?

130
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:43,231
Hey, take a closer look.

131
00:08:43,314 --> 00:08:45,275
-Director Kim.
-Yeah?

132
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:48,111
What, should we start another meeting now?

133
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:52,991
Wait… Start another meeting with you?
No, I'd rather…

134
00:08:57,871 --> 00:08:59,122
Oh, boy.

135
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:01,458
Bongsu.

136
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:03,126
Bongsu!

137
00:09:04,961 --> 00:09:06,171
[in English] Good night.

138
00:09:09,758 --> 00:09:10,884
[in Korean] Geez.

139
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:24,814
NOTICE REGARDING THE SALE OF LAND

140
00:09:24,898 --> 00:09:30,862
FARMLAND IN JAPAN REGISTERED
UNDER THE LATE LEE GYEONGSU…

141
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,781
What is this? "Land sale"?

142
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:35,283
"Charo Island"?

143
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:39,871
KARIN'S STRAWBERRIES

144
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:42,832
[Karin, in English] Good morning.
Long time no see.

145
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:44,501
-How are things?
-Good morning.

146
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,419
Nice sweet potato harvest this year.

147
00:09:46,503 --> 00:09:49,464
Yes, good morning! Mrs. Osono.

148
00:09:49,547 --> 00:09:51,299
Freshly-harvested sweet potatoes.

149
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:53,635
Oh, Karin! Good morning!

150
00:09:53,718 --> 00:09:55,970
Good morning.
Here's a free sample just for you.

151
00:09:56,054 --> 00:09:58,181
Your berries are ripe already?

152
00:09:58,264 --> 00:10:01,017
And we're introducing
a new variety next year.

153
00:10:01,101 --> 00:10:04,229
When we do,
please put them front and center.

154
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:06,856
You're certainly very skilled.

155
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:09,109
I hope that everything
goes well for you this season.

156
00:10:09,192 --> 00:10:12,904
You know I'll bring you the best ones.
Be on the lookout, all right?

157
00:10:13,488 --> 00:10:16,199
[shop owner] I've heard that one
a few too many times.

158
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:20,745
Why bother with this variety?
Doesn't even flower.

159
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:33,258
With our strawberries, we ensure that
Mother Nature ripens them naturally.

160
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:36,386
They're more delicious
than any strawberry you've tasted.

161
00:10:38,513 --> 00:10:41,599
Even if they take time more and effort,
that's precisely why

162
00:10:41,683 --> 00:10:43,101
ours are the best ones.

163
00:10:43,852 --> 00:10:45,854
Oh, someone is cocky
about her berries, huh?

164
00:10:45,937 --> 00:10:47,355
You wanna bet on it?

165
00:10:49,232 --> 00:10:51,734
Uh… I've got deliveries to run.

166
00:10:54,696 --> 00:10:58,491
You're as strong-willed as ever, dear.

167
00:10:58,575 --> 00:11:01,703
Hey, once my strawberries have been
officially certified,

168
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:05,039
then it's gonna be all over
for everybody else.

169
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:10,378
No! I'm not doing this!

170
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:12,505
-Hey, wait!
-Let go of me.

171
00:11:12,589 --> 00:11:14,382
What matters here is the model, okay?

172
00:11:14,465 --> 00:11:16,050
Hey. Dang it!

173
00:11:16,843 --> 00:11:18,303
Why's my hair looking like this?

174
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:20,597
And what's with that giant fan?

175
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:21,723
Huh?

176
00:11:21,806 --> 00:11:24,017
-[fan whirring]
-[director] Hey, hey!

177
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:26,352
Cut, cut.

178
00:11:26,436 --> 00:11:27,854
Oh, shoot, this is…

179
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:29,189
My hair…

180
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:31,482
Shoot.

181
00:11:36,154 --> 00:11:37,614
-Oh, boy.
-[huffs]

182
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:44,954
Hey, don't look at things like that.
"Y:SPACE is taking the world by storm."

183
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:49,250
Look, we don't need
any models or celebrities.

184
00:11:49,334 --> 00:11:51,961
We need an ad with your face on it

185
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:53,796
to attract investors more easily.

186
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,882
How many times
do I have to tell you, boss?

187
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:59,344
-Don't you… Ow. Don't you trust me?
-I'm not doing it.

188
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:01,012
[huffs] Come on.

189
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:04,557
Hey, you're the CEO.
The face of this company!

190
00:12:04,641 --> 00:12:06,726
Our star! Okay?

191
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:08,478
Not happening.

192
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,813
Swedish furniture.

193
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:14,400
[Yubin whines] Swedish furniture…

194
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:17,070
If this goes well, you might
finally get to collaborate

195
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:20,823
with that Swedish luxury furniture brand
you were talking about, you know.

196
00:12:20,907 --> 00:12:22,909
And if we go into
next month's meeting with this ad,

197
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:24,577
we'll make a better impression.

198
00:12:26,955 --> 00:12:27,997
I get it.

199
00:12:28,623 --> 00:12:29,832
This is new to you.

200
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:31,876
You're uncomfortable.

201
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:35,588
But just bite the bullet and think,
"This is for the future of our company,"

202
00:12:36,339 --> 00:12:37,840
and give it a go.

203
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:40,468
They said once they touch it all up
with CGI, it'll look amazing.

204
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:42,428
[crew member] All right, Yubin.
Please stand by.

205
00:12:42,512 --> 00:12:44,055
Oh, yeah, he's coming!

206
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:48,643
The gorgeous superstar Lee Yubin
is on his way! He's coming!

207
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,645
[chuckles] Yep, he's on his way.

208
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:07,954
[Yubin] <i>Where every moment you stay</i>
<i>comes alive.</i>

209
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:11,791
SPACE is taking the world by storm.

210
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:14,669
A space made just for you…

211
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:16,504
[grunts] Shoot.

212
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:17,588
SPACE.

213
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:21,801
Smile, Yubin! Smile!

214
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:25,805
Dang it!

215
00:13:25,888 --> 00:13:27,473
THE TWO FACES
OF A STAR SPATIAL DESIGNER

216
00:13:27,557 --> 00:13:28,558
SPACE IS DONE FOR

217
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:30,393
THE POPULAR PLANNER,
JUST A FIGUREHEAD ALL ALONG

218
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:31,519
WAS HE A CON ARTIST ALL ALONG?!

219
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:36,691
[reporter] <i>Lee Yubin, an internationally</i>
<i>award-winning spatial designer,</i>

220
00:13:36,774 --> 00:13:38,818
<i>has recently become embroiled</i>
<i>in fraud allegations</i>

221
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:41,154
<i>related to an urban redevelopment project.</i>

222
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:42,488
RECENTS
KIM BONGSU

223
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:47,368
[automated voice] <i>The number</i>
<i>you have dialed is not in service.</i>

224
00:13:47,452 --> 00:13:49,746
<i>Please check the number and try again.</i>

225
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:52,790
Kim Bongsu!

226
00:13:52,874 --> 00:13:55,084
How can we tell you anything
when nothing's confirmed?

227
00:13:55,168 --> 00:13:57,211
No, it's not like that.
Please just leave your number.

228
00:13:57,295 --> 00:14:03,217
-But we're not…
-We cannot speak on this matter.

229
00:14:03,301 --> 00:14:05,511
It's a surprise to us too.
So how can we tell you anything?

230
00:14:05,595 --> 00:14:07,055
Apparently, Director Kim
took everything and ran.

231
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:08,931
Weren't the two of them
supposed to be best friends?

232
00:14:09,015 --> 00:14:10,683
[employee] Exactly.

233
00:14:11,309 --> 00:14:12,393
What's Mr. Lee going to do?

234
00:14:12,477 --> 00:14:15,354
He was betrayed by his friend,
and now he's taking the fall. Geez.

235
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:18,566
Well, what's going
to happen to our paychecks?

236
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:23,696
-Where's Lee Yubin?
-What's going on?

237
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:28,618
[reporter] <i>It was later revealed that Kim,</i>
<i>a registered director and business partner</i>

238
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:31,871
<i>at Lee's company, Y:SPACE,</i>
<i>collected the project's advance payments</i>

239
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:33,539
<i>in multiple installments</i>
<i>before disappearing.</i>

240
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:35,249
<i>Although Lee</i>
<i>maintains that he was not involved</i>

241
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:36,918
<i>in the business side of the project,</i>

242
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:39,962
it won't be easy for him to escape
legal and moral responsibility.

243
00:14:40,046 --> 00:14:41,881
This is Kwon Gunam, IMP News.

244
00:14:45,635 --> 00:14:48,054
Huh? What the… What's going on?

245
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:51,349
Where's my paycheck?

246
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:03,319
NOTICE OF BUSINESS CLOSURE

247
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:05,404
WE THANK EVERYONE
WHO HAS SUPPORTED OUR COMPANY

248
00:15:05,488 --> 00:15:06,697
WE APOLOGIZE
FOR THIS ANNOUNCEMENT

249
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:08,324
AND ARE GRATEFUL FOR THE SUPPORT
YOU HAVE SHOWN US

250
00:15:08,407 --> 00:15:09,408
LEE YUBIN
SPACE INC.

251
00:15:23,548 --> 00:15:25,383
FOR RENT

252
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,185
Geez.

253
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:46,779
-[friend] Geez.
-[Yubin groans]

254
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:49,615
-What? Come on.
-Kim Bongsu, that jerk.

255
00:15:49,699 --> 00:15:52,201
I knew something was off.
You can tell a lot from a person's face.

256
00:15:52,285 --> 00:15:55,872
[Yubin] Couldn't you have come in
a little later? It's too early.

257
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:58,249
-Geez.
-Hey, it's broad daylight. Get up.

258
00:15:58,332 --> 00:16:00,293
How can you be so relaxed?

259
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:01,586
You sold your place with no backup plan.

260
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:02,670
TAX ACCOUNTANT
CHOI HYEJIN

261
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,547
-What are you going to do now?
-I don't know, okay? I don't!

262
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:07,550
I don't know. Everyone was up in arms,
demanding their money back.

263
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:09,760
-What choice did I have?
-Hold on.

264
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:12,180
What's with those pajamas?
Don't tell me they're designer.

265
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:13,890
Why didn't you sell those?

266
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,766
How could I sell these?
They're my dignity.

267
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:16,934
Would you sell your dignity?

268
00:16:17,018 --> 00:16:20,062
Maybe it'll take sleeping on the street
to knock some sense into you.

269
00:16:20,146 --> 00:16:21,647
[Yubin groans] Dang it.

270
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:25,318
[sighs] Whatever.

271
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:28,613
Anyway, the urgent stuff's
mostly taken care of.

272
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:31,574
I scraped together enough to pay
all the employees' severance too.

273
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:35,328
I'm completely broke now.

274
00:16:36,746 --> 00:16:38,539
Well, not completely.

275
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:41,959
What?

276
00:16:42,043 --> 00:16:44,212
Looks like you still have
some inherited assets.

277
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:45,296
Huh? Assets?

278
00:16:45,379 --> 00:16:47,298
A piece of land in Japan
under your father's name.

279
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:52,386
NOTICE REGARDING SALE OF LAND

280
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,513
Ah! Ah! Ah!

281
00:16:54,597 --> 00:16:57,433
Right! Oh, yeah.

282
00:16:57,516 --> 00:16:59,352
Oh, the land. I've got land.

283
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:02,647
Since it's overseas property,
it's a bit complicated.

284
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:03,731
Okay.

285
00:17:03,814 --> 00:17:07,526
But it's a pretty sizeable piece of land,
so if you sell it at a good price…

286
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:10,863
Hey, okay. Hang on.

287
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:12,657
So what do I do from here?

288
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,621
AKATSUKI CITY
GREEN NOVA CORPORATION

289
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:23,459
[in English] Now I'll need
the documents on your crop variety…

290
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:26,796
I marked it with a red sticky note.
Ah! I found it. Here it is.

291
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:29,549
Thank you. It's my first year here.
I'm sorry it's taking a while.

292
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:31,342
Don't worry. You can take your time.

293
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:35,096
-This is it?
-Uh-huh.

294
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:37,890
That's all the relevant documents
we need from you.

295
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:41,602
As for the next step…

296
00:17:41,686 --> 00:17:42,687
Crop inspection.

297
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,523
Yes, that's right.
You're an expert at this.

298
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:48,943
Well, this is my third year coming here,

299
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:52,280
and my third year attempt at passing this.

300
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:57,118
Uh, you seem thoroughly prepared.

301
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:59,036
That's why I'm sure that you'll succeed.

302
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:01,205
Thank you very much.

303
00:18:01,289 --> 00:18:04,625
I've heard that three years in a row now,
but I appreciate it.

304
00:18:05,585 --> 00:18:07,378
I'm terribly sorry.

305
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:09,505
[chuckles] It's no big deal.

306
00:18:09,589 --> 00:18:12,550
For some reason, I have
a really good feeling this year.

307
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:14,927
-[laughs]
-Oh, that's good.

308
00:18:15,011 --> 00:18:17,597
So it's a decent size,
and the pH of the soil is stable.

309
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:20,057
I told you.
The strawberries are very good.

310
00:18:20,141 --> 00:18:22,935
They're tart, high in natural sugar,
and have the best aroma…

311
00:18:23,019 --> 00:18:25,813
Oh, I'd say you're not
quite out of the woods yet.

312
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:27,982
I didn't see you standing there.

313
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:30,276
You nearly scared me half to death, sir.

314
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:33,738
Paperwork is easy. It's the crop
inspection that really gets you.

315
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:36,115
-You know that?
-I'm well aware and prepared.

316
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:39,368
I've seen my grandfather
go through this process again and again.

317
00:18:39,452 --> 00:18:42,330
Quiz. Tagawa, off the top of your head,

318
00:18:42,413 --> 00:18:46,083
tell me what it takes to pass
crop inspection. Let's hear it, kid.

319
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:51,130
Over 80% of the field, uh,
must bear fruit.

320
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:54,508
Also, the consistency of the fruit's size,

321
00:18:54,592 --> 00:18:56,927
its firmness and sweetness,

322
00:18:57,011 --> 00:18:59,388
must match what's listed
in the submitted paperwork.

323
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:01,641
Oh. There you have it.

324
00:19:01,724 --> 00:19:03,726
-[sigh]
-[Karin chuckles]

325
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:05,645
Well, feel free to stop by anytime.

326
00:19:05,728 --> 00:19:07,772
I'll show you the best strawberries
you'll ever taste.

327
00:19:09,774 --> 00:19:11,442
I'd be happy to come by.

328
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:15,488
You're going to surpass your grandfather
as a farmer if you keep going like that.

329
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:19,992
So I'll see you in three days
for the crop inspection.

330
00:19:20,076 --> 00:19:22,662
Great. I'm looking forward to it.

331
00:19:22,745 --> 00:19:24,997
Oh! I'm gonna miss the ferry!
See you later.

332
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:26,791
-Thank you as always!
-Have a nice ride back.

333
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:28,042
Bye!

334
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:34,799
FUKUOKA PIER - FERRY TERMINAL 1

335
00:19:34,882 --> 00:19:36,175
[Yubin] Thank you.

336
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:43,349
[in Korean] Hey, they only run
three ferries a day to the island.

337
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:44,934
How tiny is this place?

338
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:47,269
<i>You got all the paperwork ready, right?</i>

339
00:19:47,353 --> 00:19:50,898
Yeah. I'll just take one last look around
and head straight back.

340
00:19:50,981 --> 00:19:53,609
<i>Why? Since you're there,</i>
<i>why not stay and relax for a bit?</i>

341
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:57,947
Hey, are you kidding me? What's there
to do on that tiny little island?

342
00:19:58,030 --> 00:20:00,241
[announcer, in English] <i>Dear passengers,</i>
<i>the ferry bound for Charo Island…</i>

343
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:03,202
-[in Korean] I think it's here. Gotta go.
-[in English] <i>…will disembark momentarily.</i>

344
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:05,788
<i>If you have not boarded the ferry yet</i>
<i>please gather…</i>

345
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:07,873
-Charo Island, please.
-Charo Island.

346
00:20:07,957 --> 00:20:09,583
Oh. [chuckles]

347
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,129
This is the last ticket.

348
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:14,380
-What?
-Huh?

349
00:20:14,463 --> 00:20:17,049
Is he saying there's only one ticket left?

350
00:20:17,133 --> 00:20:20,177
[in English] Uh, do you mind
if I buy the last ticket?

351
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:23,514
[in Korean] Sorry? No, I mean…
What's she saying?

352
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:26,225
[in English] I-- I'm Korean.

353
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:29,562
-I'm sorry.
-Oh. You're Korean… [stammers]

354
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:34,692
[clears throat] I'm in a hurry.
Could you let me buy the ticket?

355
00:20:38,988 --> 00:20:42,575
[in Korean] I'm really sorry, but I've got
something important too. I'm sorry.

356
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:52,001
[in English] I'm not feeling so great.
Could I…

357
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:54,503
[in Korean] What?
You were sprinting just fine a second ago.

358
00:20:58,966 --> 00:21:00,676
[in English] Well, I was here first,
before you.

359
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:02,887
But I touched the counter first.

360
00:21:08,976 --> 00:21:10,811
<i>Rock, scissors, paper.</i>

361
00:21:12,521 --> 00:21:13,981
-Huh?
-Rock, scissors, paper…

362
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:15,775
[in Korean] Rock… Rock, paper, scissors?

363
00:21:15,858 --> 00:21:17,401
-Hurry up.
-No, come on.

364
00:21:17,485 --> 00:21:20,237
We're not actually doing rock,
paper, scissors for a ticket, are we?

365
00:21:20,321 --> 00:21:21,530
[in English] Give up?

366
00:21:22,031 --> 00:21:23,115
"Give up"?

367
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:25,743
-[in Korean] Rock, paper, scissors!
-[in English] Hey, I wasn't ready.

368
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:36,796
[Yubin thinking, in Korean] <i>Welcome to</i>
<i>the ruthless world of competition.</i>

369
00:21:58,818 --> 00:22:00,236
[in English] Ready, go.

370
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:01,320
Ready, go.

371
00:22:07,785 --> 00:22:12,206
[in Korean] Ugh! I should've thrown rock!
I should've…

372
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:15,668
Hey, listen. In Korea, we do best two
out of three. One more round, please.

373
00:22:15,751 --> 00:22:18,963
[in English] Welcome to
the cutthroat world of competition, sir.

374
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:24,093
EXIT

375
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:26,220
Oh, it's Daniel!

376
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:28,013
Daniel! Daniel!

377
00:22:29,098 --> 00:22:31,100
Daniel! Hang on.

378
00:22:31,183 --> 00:22:32,852
You can't leave yet!

379
00:22:34,895 --> 00:22:37,690
I'm sorry. I can't stay any longer.

380
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:42,278
No, Daniel, you can't go.
I need you to stay here.

381
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:43,863
-I can't do it by myself.
-Not my problem.

382
00:22:44,697 --> 00:22:46,866
-Daniel, please…
-Let go!

383
00:22:46,949 --> 00:22:49,201
You have to stay! I need you!

384
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:52,121
You're the strongest man I've ever met
in my entire life!

385
00:22:52,204 --> 00:22:53,664
What?

386
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:55,082
[in Korean] What is she doing?

387
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:58,627
[in English] You beg me every day
to go harder and put my muscle into it.

388
00:22:58,711 --> 00:23:01,130
I don't have the stamina
to do what you want.

389
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:04,967
-Please, don't leave me.
-[in Korean] Wow, she's intense.

390
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:07,595
[Karin, in English] Is it money?
I'll give you so much money…

391
00:23:07,678 --> 00:23:08,762
How much do you want?

392
00:23:08,846 --> 00:23:10,139
I don't want anything.

393
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:13,392
-Give it to me.
-Please. Think this over.

394
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:16,061
Don't be rash. Stay. I need you. Stay!

395
00:23:16,145 --> 00:23:17,771
[grunts] Stay!

396
00:23:25,154 --> 00:23:26,655
You cheated!

397
00:23:26,739 --> 00:23:28,073
-Daniel, please!
-Let me go!

398
00:23:28,866 --> 00:23:31,076
[Karin] <i>Don't leave!</i>

399
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:35,748
"Could I have a copy of the plat map?"

400
00:23:35,831 --> 00:23:37,124
Could I have a copy of…

401
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:38,626
COULD I HAVE A COPY
OF THE PLAT MAP?

402
00:23:38,709 --> 00:23:40,502
"Could I have a copy of the plat map?"

403
00:23:43,339 --> 00:23:44,715
"Could I…"

404
00:23:44,798 --> 00:23:45,925
Oh, uh…

405
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:02,858
I don't even like these anymore.

406
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:07,029
Just one a day, okay?

407
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:10,491
Don't eat like a dozen and get an earful
from your mom again like last time.

408
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:13,994
Have you been guarding her well
while I was away?

409
00:24:14,078 --> 00:24:15,412
Guarding her?

410
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:18,248
What am I, a dog?

411
00:24:20,042 --> 00:24:21,794
Hey, are you already
going through puberty?

412
00:24:25,589 --> 00:24:28,342
You'll be working here in Korea
for a while, right?

413
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:40,229
I've got to go back in a week.

414
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:41,772
And this time, I'll be away a bit longer.

415
00:24:44,692 --> 00:24:45,901
Why don't you just move there?

416
00:25:00,916 --> 00:25:02,876
They still make these, huh?

417
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:04,837
[in English] Where did my candy go?

418
00:25:05,421 --> 00:25:06,755
Under here?

419
00:25:06,839 --> 00:25:07,881
It's not there.

420
00:25:07,965 --> 00:25:09,299
[in Korean] Looking for this?

421
00:25:10,718 --> 00:25:13,137
[in English] Thank you very much.

422
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:15,597
Thank you very much. [chuckles]

423
00:25:26,066 --> 00:25:27,985
[in Korean] I'll just sell it off
and be done with it.

424
00:25:28,569 --> 00:25:29,945
Should be simple enough.

425
00:25:31,989 --> 00:25:33,949
[in English] It's not that easy.

426
00:25:34,533 --> 00:25:37,369
Please, sir.
Can you really not find anyone?

427
00:25:37,453 --> 00:25:40,414
I asked around, but no one's available.

428
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:42,916
No one who wants to work
on your farm, anyway.

429
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:44,001
Huh? Why not?

430
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:47,713
The work is physically demanding,
there's nothing to do on the island,

431
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:50,466
and they're all terrified of the owner.

432
00:25:50,549 --> 00:25:52,718
What? They think that I'm--

433
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:55,220
Oh, whatever. I'm nice.
I'm not terrifying at all.

434
00:25:56,013 --> 00:26:00,017
Listen, Karin, what if you call it quits?
Do something easier?

435
00:26:00,684 --> 00:26:02,853
Somebody your size
isn't made for farm work.

436
00:26:02,936 --> 00:26:04,730
[sighs] You listen.

437
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:06,690
I've worked five years on my own

438
00:26:06,774 --> 00:26:09,068
and ten with my grandfather before that.

439
00:26:09,985 --> 00:26:15,032
On top of that, if your strawberries
don't get certified this time,

440
00:26:15,115 --> 00:26:17,326
your relief aid will get pulled.

441
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:18,452
Aren't you worried?

442
00:26:18,535 --> 00:26:21,413
Yes, of course I am,
and that's why this whole thing matters!

443
00:26:21,497 --> 00:26:22,998
You know that as well as I do.

444
00:26:23,082 --> 00:26:24,500
Karin, calm down.

445
00:26:28,337 --> 00:26:29,755
Even so…

446
00:26:31,381 --> 00:26:34,301
finding any new employees around here,

447
00:26:34,384 --> 00:26:36,595
it's certainly not easy.

448
00:26:39,139 --> 00:26:40,390
Ah…

449
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:42,851
Hmm?

450
00:26:43,769 --> 00:26:45,771
Karin, what have you got there?

451
00:26:49,149 --> 00:26:50,275
Where'd you get that?

452
00:26:50,859 --> 00:26:52,778
It's a really expensive bottle.

453
00:26:52,861 --> 00:26:55,823
I know. It's your favorite, right?

454
00:26:59,118 --> 00:27:00,536
Whoa!

455
00:27:01,829 --> 00:27:03,705
Mmm, mmm! [chuckles]

456
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:06,041
Oh! Oh.

457
00:27:06,125 --> 00:27:08,877
So, you sure you can't find anyone?

458
00:27:09,795 --> 00:27:13,841
Well… what sort of employee
are you looking for?

459
00:27:14,341 --> 00:27:16,635
I'll make sure to find you the right fit.

460
00:27:19,972 --> 00:27:21,682
[child] He's throwing up!

461
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:26,144
Firstly, they need to be strong…

462
00:27:32,359 --> 00:27:33,360
[in Korean] What…

463
00:27:34,361 --> 00:27:36,655
Come on, how come I can't get a signal?

464
00:27:37,447 --> 00:27:39,283
Come on, give me a signal already.

465
00:27:39,366 --> 00:27:40,909
Geez! Why won't it connect?

466
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:45,622
-[in English] …a pleasant personality…
-Right.

467
00:27:46,540 --> 00:27:48,417
But as for looks…

468
00:27:54,548 --> 00:27:56,174
Anything works. Doesn't matter.

469
00:27:57,426 --> 00:28:00,345
Oh! Hello!

470
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:06,643
CHARO ISLAND VILLAGE BUS
HAMANOKUCHI - IRIE

471
00:28:06,727 --> 00:28:08,437
NEXT IS SHIOHAMA

472
00:28:18,572 --> 00:28:21,700
-The next bus isn't coming for a while.
-Hey?

473
00:28:21,783 --> 00:28:24,119
They only run three a day.
You just missed one.

474
00:28:25,245 --> 00:28:28,665
Look. See? No buses. Where you heading?

475
00:28:28,749 --> 00:28:30,292
I can give you a ride. Just hop in.

476
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:31,960
Come on.

477
00:28:34,254 --> 00:28:35,839
I don't have all day here.

478
00:28:37,174 --> 00:28:39,718
-Hurry up, would you?
-[in Korean] Wait, no more buses.

479
00:28:39,801 --> 00:28:42,304
I said I'd take you. Get in the car.

480
00:28:42,387 --> 00:28:44,932
[groans] I'm okay, thank you.

481
00:28:45,015 --> 00:28:47,017
-Get in here. Come on.
-I… Okay.

482
00:28:47,684 --> 00:28:48,852
-Hop in.
-I'm okay.

483
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:56,777
-And now it's pouring. [sighs]
-[Yubin exclaims]

484
00:28:58,028 --> 00:28:59,655
[in Korean] I'll take that ride!
I'll take it!

485
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,406
-[in English] Help. Help me, help me.
-Buckle up.

486
00:29:01,490 --> 00:29:03,116
Help me, help me.

487
00:29:25,222 --> 00:29:29,434
[in Korean] Shoot… This weather…
It's going to be okay, right?

488
00:29:34,231 --> 00:29:36,692
[in English] What are you gonna do
over at the village office?

489
00:29:37,609 --> 00:29:38,860
[in Korean] Sorry?

490
00:29:39,778 --> 00:29:41,071
Uh, uh, uh…

491
00:29:41,154 --> 00:29:42,489
Hold on.

492
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:43,949
Hold on.

493
00:29:45,242 --> 00:29:46,910
[in English] It's fine. Forget about it.

494
00:29:46,994 --> 00:29:48,412
How about some music?

495
00:30:05,178 --> 00:30:06,680
[in Korean] This feels a little off.

496
00:30:06,763 --> 00:30:08,890
MAP SEARCH

497
00:30:36,251 --> 00:30:37,377
Karin?

498
00:30:38,128 --> 00:30:40,630
-[in English] Hey, why are you still here?
-Mari!

499
00:30:40,714 --> 00:30:42,799
Ah, you're here. I'm so glad.

500
00:30:42,883 --> 00:30:45,427
You forgot to bring
your medication again, didn't you?

501
00:30:45,510 --> 00:30:49,681
That's why I tried to get home
as soon as possible, but Daniel…

502
00:30:49,765 --> 00:30:51,767
What about my sweet little Daniel?

503
00:30:53,101 --> 00:30:54,436
Huh?

504
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:57,647
Yesterday, Daniel and I, um, kind of…

505
00:30:58,648 --> 00:30:59,775
He took off.

506
00:31:01,276 --> 00:31:03,612
-What?
-Daniel quit today.

507
00:31:03,695 --> 00:31:06,239
-He went back to Germany.
-[gasps]

508
00:31:06,323 --> 00:31:10,202
[whimpers] Just when I finally
let him kiss me.

509
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:11,661
No way. Ugh.

510
00:31:11,745 --> 00:31:14,623
Is that what he was planning
to do all along?

511
00:31:14,706 --> 00:31:18,710
Is that why he kissed me so passionately?

512
00:31:18,794 --> 00:31:20,712
Oh, how annoying.

513
00:31:23,256 --> 00:31:26,384
-Hey! Wait till you're back on the island.
-Why?

514
00:31:26,468 --> 00:31:28,136
The tarot cards said
that we had a strong bond.

515
00:31:28,220 --> 00:31:31,765
-Stop! I need a drink! Come on!
-Knock it off.

516
00:31:31,848 --> 00:31:34,768
-Let go!
-Wait until we're back!

517
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:40,565
[Yubin] Whoa.

518
00:31:55,539 --> 00:31:57,999
[in English] I gotta take care
of something.

519
00:31:59,835 --> 00:32:01,628
[Yubin, in Korean] What? What is it?

520
00:32:26,069 --> 00:32:27,154
No!

521
00:32:35,120 --> 00:32:37,205
-[in English] This is a bad omen.
-Huh? What is?

522
00:32:37,914 --> 00:32:40,959
I mean, look at the cards.
The queen represents you.

523
00:32:41,042 --> 00:32:43,253
At first, you seem frail.

524
00:32:43,336 --> 00:32:45,463
-But you're resilient deep down.
-Mm-hmm.

525
00:32:45,547 --> 00:32:49,176
Seven of Cups represents
a situation with way too many choices.

526
00:32:49,885 --> 00:32:52,846
It could be a fantasy,
or it could become reality.

527
00:32:53,805 --> 00:32:54,806
Is that a bad thing?

528
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:58,018
The outcome would be up to you, my friend.

529
00:32:58,101 --> 00:33:01,855
-Tarot cards are such a sham.
-You need to believe in it, Karin.

530
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:05,192
Why? They were wrong about Daniel, right?

531
00:33:05,275 --> 00:33:07,235
They didn't predict him leaving.

532
00:33:08,653 --> 00:33:10,906
It's easiest to miss
what's right under your nose.

533
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:16,703
[chuckles] Tell me
what this shiny one means.

534
00:33:17,245 --> 00:33:19,039
[gasps] It's the Wheel…

535
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:21,666
of Fortune.

536
00:33:23,585 --> 00:33:25,962
It means you're bound
to have a fated encounter

537
00:33:26,046 --> 00:33:28,465
camouflaged as a coincidence
in the near future.

538
00:33:35,180 --> 00:33:36,723
It means fate?

539
00:33:43,521 --> 00:33:45,690
[in Korean] Where am I?

540
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,237
[groans] I'm screwed.
My phone's dying too.

541
00:33:54,157 --> 00:33:55,992
[sighs] I'm screwed.

542
00:33:57,661 --> 00:33:58,662
I'm screwed.

543
00:34:01,289 --> 00:34:03,041
I left all my stuff back there.

544
00:34:11,216 --> 00:34:12,217
Dang it!

545
00:34:17,097 --> 00:34:18,598
[in English] Excuse me!

546
00:34:18,682 --> 00:34:19,933
[in Korean] Hey!

547
00:34:23,144 --> 00:34:24,854
Come on, seriously.

548
00:34:25,939 --> 00:34:28,275
[groans] This place is just not for me.

549
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:45,375
[in English] Why did you run away?

550
00:34:46,543 --> 00:34:47,544
Huh?

551
00:35:02,058 --> 00:35:04,185
CHARO VILLAGE OFFICE

552
00:35:04,269 --> 00:35:06,229
[Yubin] Thank you so much.

553
00:35:06,313 --> 00:35:09,190
-Thank you so much.
-Huh. Strange.

554
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:13,236
Karin already lives
on the plot of land that you own.

555
00:35:14,362 --> 00:35:16,698
It's better to go
and have yourselves a little chat.

556
00:35:17,324 --> 00:35:20,535
-Uh--
-Uh, you don't understand.

557
00:35:22,746 --> 00:35:25,582
Hey, Kunam, you know where Karin lives.

558
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:27,542
-Can you give this guy a ride?
-[gasps]

559
00:35:38,094 --> 00:35:39,387
Oh…

560
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:48,355
Here we are.

561
00:35:55,278 --> 00:35:56,571
Thank you very much.

562
00:35:58,156 --> 00:35:59,741
Thank you very much.

563
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,827
-Are you all right?
-Huh?

564
00:36:08,750 --> 00:36:11,002
I think I'm right about this.

565
00:36:14,923 --> 00:36:17,050
[shouting, in Korean] Oh, my God…

566
00:36:23,098 --> 00:36:25,517
[in broken Korean] "Oh, my God."
[in English] Is that right?

567
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:28,603
[chuckles] "Oh, my God, Oh, my God"
in Korean?

568
00:36:36,820 --> 00:36:38,530
[in Korean] Right? Yeah?

569
00:36:39,114 --> 00:36:41,408
Come on, I knew it. You're Korean.

570
00:36:42,659 --> 00:36:43,660
[in English] I don't…

571
00:36:46,955 --> 00:36:49,040
-[in Korean] You're right. I am.
-Geez.

572
00:36:49,124 --> 00:36:52,419
Can I get your number?
I think I'm going to need your help.

573
00:36:52,502 --> 00:36:54,963
I don't really speak
the language here, so… Yeah?

574
00:36:57,632 --> 00:36:59,008
[in English] What a pain.

575
00:36:59,592 --> 00:37:00,802
[in Korean] All right, thanks.

576
00:37:02,679 --> 00:37:04,889
-[phone buzzing]
-Calling. [in English] Okay.

577
00:37:06,474 --> 00:37:08,977
Okay. Block.

578
00:37:13,106 --> 00:37:16,067
-[in Korean] I know what "blocked" means.
-Feel free to call me, sir.

579
00:37:31,374 --> 00:37:32,459
So is this it?

580
00:37:35,462 --> 00:37:36,713
What's that?

581
00:37:40,592 --> 00:37:42,177
STRAWBERRY PICKING
KAMINOSAWA FARM

582
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:43,678
ALL YOU CAN EAT

583
00:37:43,762 --> 00:37:45,138
-[in English] Hey…
-Huh?

584
00:37:45,889 --> 00:37:47,265
I was thinking…

585
00:37:47,849 --> 00:37:50,769
What if the tarot cards were
describing my strawberries?

586
00:37:50,852 --> 00:37:54,063
Strawberries?
That would be sad, don't you think?

587
00:37:54,147 --> 00:37:58,026
Sad? Why? I spent three years
tending to my precious strawberries,

588
00:37:58,109 --> 00:38:00,069
and now they're finally getting
recognition.

589
00:38:00,153 --> 00:38:02,322
-[sighs]
-I couldn't be prouder of them.

590
00:38:02,405 --> 00:38:05,533
You think your strawberries
have personalities?

591
00:38:05,617 --> 00:38:08,077
-Yeah, in some ways, they--
-Mari, you're here.

592
00:38:09,078 --> 00:38:11,331
Ooh. What great timing.

593
00:38:14,751 --> 00:38:16,669
-I'll hold it.
-Thank you.

594
00:38:17,670 --> 00:38:20,757
Didn't I tell you?
Kunam is totally head over heels for you.

595
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:23,968
[chuckles] Yeah, well,
he's not my type at all.

596
00:38:24,803 --> 00:38:26,805
Do you want to get dinner together?

597
00:38:26,888 --> 00:38:29,015
-Karin, do you wanna come too?
-I can join?

598
00:38:29,098 --> 00:38:31,309
-Mm-hmm.
-I almost forgot!

599
00:38:31,392 --> 00:38:34,020
There's some guy waiting for you
at your place.

600
00:38:34,729 --> 00:38:36,648
Who is it? Do you know? What guy?

601
00:38:36,731 --> 00:38:37,899
Maybe Daniel's replacement?

602
00:38:37,982 --> 00:38:41,277
-Not that quickly. No way.
-What did he look like? Was he hot?

603
00:38:41,361 --> 00:38:44,072
Was he hot? Not hotter than me. Come on.

604
00:38:47,408 --> 00:38:48,827
Sorry, Mari. I've gotta check.

605
00:38:48,910 --> 00:38:50,537
-See you later.
-What? Hey, wait!

606
00:38:53,915 --> 00:38:55,583
It's just us.

607
00:38:57,460 --> 00:38:59,087
Sure. Why not?

608
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:00,296
Come on.

609
00:39:01,506 --> 00:39:02,507
Yay!

610
00:39:04,342 --> 00:39:05,885
[Yubin] "Karin Farm"?

611
00:39:10,098 --> 00:39:11,349
[in Korean] What is this?

612
00:39:16,354 --> 00:39:18,439
Wait, is someone living here or what?

613
00:39:19,148 --> 00:39:20,316
Is this a farm?

614
00:39:21,943 --> 00:39:23,945
Wait, what the hell's going on here?

615
00:39:36,291 --> 00:39:37,625
Is someone living here?

616
00:39:43,923 --> 00:39:45,758
[teacher, in English] Slow down! Careful!

617
00:39:45,842 --> 00:39:47,427
Don't lose your buddy!

618
00:39:50,263 --> 00:39:53,600
Excuse me. Can you tell me
where the strawberry picking is?

619
00:39:53,683 --> 00:39:56,144
Over there? Or here?

620
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:57,812
Uh… [speaks Japanese]

621
00:39:57,896 --> 00:39:59,981
-[in Korean] What?
-[in English] Right there!

622
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:02,066
Yay! Strawberries!

623
00:40:02,150 --> 00:40:04,068
[teacher] Be careful down the stairs!

624
00:40:06,821 --> 00:40:08,573
[child] Look at this one!

625
00:40:09,157 --> 00:40:11,367
-[in Korean] Well, this is…
-[child, in English] Over here!

626
00:40:12,452 --> 00:40:14,871
[in Korean] Is this one of those
strawberry-picking places?

627
00:40:18,541 --> 00:40:20,627
-[in English] Karin.
-Oh, you're back!

628
00:40:20,710 --> 00:40:23,171
-I'm back.
-So how was it? Will you pass this year?

629
00:40:23,254 --> 00:40:25,715
Mm-hmm. Green Nova is coming
to inspect in three days,

630
00:40:25,798 --> 00:40:27,467
but I feel good about it.

631
00:40:29,510 --> 00:40:32,305
<i>If 80% of my crop bears fruit,</i>
<i>then I'll pass.</i>

632
00:40:34,682 --> 00:40:36,017
I've got this!

633
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:37,226
-That's good.
-That's great to hear.

634
00:40:37,310 --> 00:40:38,311
[Karin] Right?

635
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:44,275
Ah!

636
00:40:44,359 --> 00:40:46,486
-Here.
-[in Korean] Oh, these?

637
00:40:50,239 --> 00:40:51,824
[in English] Thank you very much.

638
00:40:54,327 --> 00:40:55,745
[in Korean] Okay.

639
00:41:04,671 --> 00:41:05,672
Mmm.

640
00:41:09,342 --> 00:41:11,719
-[in English] Hi there.
-[child] Hello.

641
00:41:11,803 --> 00:41:14,055
-[chuckles] Hi.
-Hello.

642
00:41:14,138 --> 00:41:15,431
Hello.

643
00:41:16,099 --> 00:41:17,225
[child] Yay!

644
00:41:41,457 --> 00:41:43,459
What happened? What…

645
00:41:47,797 --> 00:41:50,466
What? This can't be…

646
00:41:52,093 --> 00:41:53,094
What?

647
00:41:57,849 --> 00:42:01,477
Over 80% of the field, uh,
must bear fruit.

648
00:42:09,318 --> 00:42:11,487
[agency owner] <i>On top of that,</i>

649
00:42:11,571 --> 00:42:14,532
<i>if your strawberries</i>
<i>don't get certified this time,</i>

650
00:42:15,241 --> 00:42:17,410
then your relief aid will get pulled.

651
00:42:17,493 --> 00:42:19,037
Are you sure you're not worried?

652
00:42:34,927 --> 00:42:36,846
[in Korean] Are you the owner of…

653
00:42:38,431 --> 00:42:39,474
Huh?

654
00:42:41,768 --> 00:42:43,561
[in English] What are you doing?

655
00:43:32,777 --> 00:43:34,028
MERRY BERRY LOVE

656
00:43:34,112 --> 00:43:35,113
NEXT EPISODE

657
00:43:35,196 --> 00:43:39,075
<i>You walked onto my private property</i>
<i>and you single-handedly ruined everything.</i>

658
00:43:39,909 --> 00:43:41,869
You're the new field worker?

659
00:43:41,953 --> 00:43:44,205
[Karin] <i>He doesn't look like</i>
<i>he's touched dirt in his entire life.</i>

660
00:43:44,288 --> 00:43:48,209
[Yubin, in Korean] <i>People fight.</i>
<i>That's how you get close and build a bond.</i>
